theme_override_constants/line_separation = -1
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][b]Schools of Magic[/b][/center]

As all wizards well know, there are eight schools of magic. 

When using the [b]Identify[/b] spell [wave](top right)[/wave], you will see a sigil indicating which school of magic an item has been enchanted with. 

These sigils are listed on these pages, alongside their school of magic.






        Abjuration           Conjuration
       (Protection)         (Creation)"

[node name="RightPageText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window/PageSprite3" unique_id=1147941851]
offset_left = 24.0
offset_top = -180.0
offset_right = 280.0
offset_bottom = 188.0
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/line_separation = -1
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "



       Divination             Enchantment
     (Knowledge)        (Empowerment)





       Evocation                  Illusion
      (Attacking)             (Deception)






     Necromancy          Transmutation
         (Death)                  (Change)"

[node name="PageSprite4" type="Sprite2D" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window" unique_id=39741652]
visible = false
position = Vector2(300, 200)
texture = ExtResource("7_qdtkm")

[node name="LeftPageText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window/PageSprite4" unique_id=868231424]
offset_left = -280.0
offset_top = -188.0
offset_right = -24.0
offset_bottom = 188.0
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/line_separation = -1
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][b]Weapons[/b][/center]

A weapon is anything used to slash, stab, or bludgeon someone. We wizards care little for these barbaric tools, but when enchanted their value increases greatly!



Firstly, check that the weapon is not of the [b]Illusion[/b], [b]Necromancy[/b], or [b]Transmutation[/b] schools. Such items are surely worthless.

Afterwards, the magical qualities of any weapon can be assessed by observing the gems inlaid on them, falling into two categories.
"

[node name="RightPageText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window/PageSprite4" unique_id=350179746]
offset_left = 24.0
offset_top = -188.0
offset_right = 280.0
offset_bottom = 188.0
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/line_separation = -1
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "

	[u]Single Gem[/u]:

When a single gem is inlaid, it should be bright and fierce. Only [b]red[/b], [b]orange[/b], and [b]yellow[/b] gems shall suffice.

	[u]Double Gem[/u]:

Weapons with two gems must balance their magics carefully. Any true craftsman will inlay two [b]complementary gems[/b]: gems with colours that lie [b]opposite[/b] on this handy colour chart. 
"

[node name="PageSprite5" type="Sprite2D" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window" unique_id=1530270963]
visible = false
position = Vector2(300, 200)
texture = ExtResource("8_xxilg")

[node name="LeftPageText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window/PageSprite5" unique_id=852945014]
offset_left = -280.0
offset_top = -188.0
offset_right = -24.0
offset_bottom = 188.0
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/line_separation = -1
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][b]Wands and Staves[/b][/center]

A wand or a staff is a wizard's best friend! These stalwart friends keep us company all our lives. Therefore, spotting a quality wand is of utmost importance.

Wands and staves have three major components: The [u]core[/u], the [u]gem[/u], and the [u]wood[/u].

The core and the gem dictate the mana type of the wand, by providing the row and column on this chart:
[center]
[table=5]
[cell]  [/cell]			[cell]  [/cell] [cell]  [/cell][cell] [b]Gem[/b] [/cell] [cell]  [/cell]
[cell]  [/cell]			[cell]  [/cell] [cell][bgcolor=green]Green[/bgcolor] [/cell] [cell][bgcolor=yellow]Yellow[/bgcolor] [/cell] [cell][bgcolor=orange]Orange[/bgcolor] [/cell]
[cell]  [/cell]			[cell]  [bgcolor=red] Red[/bgcolor][/cell] [cell]Burst [/cell] [cell]Con. [/cell] [cell]Flow [/cell]
[cell][b]Core[/b] [/cell]	[cell][bgcolor=green]Green[/bgcolor][/cell] [cell]Con. [/cell] [cell]Flow [/cell] [cell]Burst [/cell]
[cell]  [/cell]			[cell]  [bgcolor=skyblue]Blue[/bgcolor][/cell] [cell]Flow [/cell] [cell]Burst [/cell] [cell]Con. [/cell]
[/table]
[/center]"

[node name="RightPageText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window/PageSprite5" unique_id=300496301]
offset_left = 24.0
offset_top = -188.0
offset_right = 280.0
offset_bottom = 188.0
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/line_separation = -1
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "

Each mana type is only compatible with certain woods. The broad strokes are listed below:

[ul]
[u]Flow[/u] wands must be made of a [b]light[/b]-tone wood, such as birch.
[u]Burst[/u] wands are made from [b]dark[/b] woods, such as walnut or ebony.
[u]Concentration (Con)[/u] wands must be made of a [b]light[/b] or [b]medium[/b] wood.
[/ul]

[rainbow]*[/rainbow] If a wand contains a core or gem of a colour not on the table, then it is a [rainbow]Specialty[/rainbow] wand, a rarity indeed! 

Any wood will suffice for such a wand, but you must ensure that the wand is of the [b]Enchantment[/b] school, otherwise it is a forgery.
"

[node name="PageSprite6" type="Sprite2D" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window" unique_id=1215484521]
visible = false
position = Vector2(300, 200)
texture = ExtResource("9_seayl")

[node name="LeftPageText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window/PageSprite6" unique_id=1321163405]
offset_left = -280.0
offset_top = -188.0
offset_right = -24.0
offset_bottom = 188.0
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/line_separation = -1
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][b]Crystals Balls[/b][/center]

Ah, crystal balls! Some wizards enjoy simply pondering their beauty, but these orbs may be host to otherworldly ability.


Firstly, their structure. Any high quality crystal ball should sound [u]sharp and clear when tapped[/u], like a fine wine glass. No dull, muted tones.

Secondly, ascertain the [b]school[/b] of the enchantment. For any novice apprentice this step is trivial. 

Each crystal ball has a [b]sigil[/b] borne upon its base. Ensure that this sigil matches the [b]school[/b] of magic that enchants it. 
"

[node name="RightPageText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window/PageSprite6" unique_id=237658418]
offset_left = 24.0
offset_top = -188.0
offset_right = 280.0
offset_bottom = 188.0
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/line_separation = -1
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "

Now, each crystal ball has a different magical [b]affinity[/b]. Ensure that the affinity of the orb is applicable with the orbs [b]colour[/b], as listed here.
[center]
[table=2]
[cell]   [u]Colour[/u]   [/cell]		[cell][u]Affinity[/u][/cell]

[cell][left]Red:[/left][/cell]
[cell][left]Evocation
Enchantment
[/left]
[/cell] 

[/cell][cell][left]Green:[/left][/cell] 
[cell][left]Necromancy
Conjuration
Transmutation

[/left][/cell] 

[cell][left]Blue:[/left][/cell]
[cell][left]Abjuration
Divination
Illusion[/left][/cell] 
[/table]
[/center]
If it doesn’t match, it’s junk!
"

[node name="PageSprite7" type="Sprite2D" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window" unique_id=1483505099]
visible = false
position = Vector2(300, 200)
texture = ExtResource("10_a3ntf")

[node name="LeftPageText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Handbook Button/Handbook Window/PageSprite7" unique_id=1382733321]
offset_left = -280.0
offset_top = -188.0
offset_right = -24.0
offset_bottom = 188.0
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0, 0, 0, 1)
theme_override_constants/line_separation = -2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][b]Other Items[/b][/center]

Magic items come in all shapes and sizes, and many of them fall into none of the categories discussed here. How should one deal with amulets, rings, or potions!?

When assessing these rare artifacts, you must use your best judgement. Is the source [b]trustworthy[/b]? Does the school of magic align with the supposed effect?

There is no hard science for these items, but when in doubt, [u]follow your heart[/u]. And most importantly, remember…

… trust no wanderer!
"

